241
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:28,160
applied to create a gradient along the

242
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:30,240
axis. Meaning the field is slightly

243
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:32,720
stronger at one end and weaker at the

244
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:34,560
other. Since the law frequency depends

245
00:09:32,720 --> 00:09:36,560
on field strength, different positions

246
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:39,279
along the tube correspond to different

247
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:41,680
procession frequencies.

248
00:09:39,279 --> 00:09:43,279
For example, at a position 1.3 m down

249
00:09:41,680 --> 00:09:46,080
the tube, the magnetic field might be

250
00:09:43,279 --> 00:09:48,080
B1, slightly larger than B 0.

251
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:51,040
Substituting B1 into the equation, you

252
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:52,959
