561
00:21:52,720 --> 00:21:56,880
shell, we have electrons moving around.

562
00:21:55,200 --> 00:21:59,360
In reality, their positions are

563
00:21:56,880 --> 00:22:02,720
described by probabilities, but we often

564
00:21:59,360 --> 00:22:04,640
picture them as orbiting the nucleus.

565
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:06,480
Inside the nucleus, we find two main

566
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:08,960
types of particles, protons and

567
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:10,960
neutrons. Protons carry positive

568
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:12,640
charges, while neutrons are electrically

569
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:14,720
neutral.

570
00:22:12,640 --> 00:22:16,799
Since all the protons are positively

571
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:19,120
charged, they would naturally repel each

572
00:22:16,799 --> 00:22:21,360
other. But they are held together by the

573
00:22:19,120 --> 00:22:23,200
strong nuclear force which balances out

574
00:22:21,360 --> 00:22:26,080
the electromagnetic repulsion and

575
00:22:23,200 --> 00:22:28,080
creates a stable nucleus.

576
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:30,960
This balance of forces is what allows

577
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:33,280
atoms to exist in a stable form. And it

578
00:22:30,960 --> 00:22:35,679
is precisely these nuclear properties,

579
00:22:33,280 --> 00:22:38,159
especially the behavior of protons that

580
00:22:35,679 --> 00:22:40,640
are central to MRI. Because the hydrogen

581
00:22:38,159 --> 00:22:42,799
nucleus, which is just a single proton,

582
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:46,280
is the main source of signal in magnetic

583
00:22:42,799 --> 00:22:46,280
resonance imaging.

584
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:52,240
Now, let's focus on the proton itself. A

585
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:54,000
proton is a positively charged particle,

586
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:56,559
and one of its most important properties

587
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:58,799
is spin. You can think of spin as being

588
00:22:56,559 --> 00:23:00,559
similar to a tiny top rotating on its

589
00:22:58,799 --> 00:23:02,480
axis.

590
00:23:00,559 --> 00:23:04,000
Because the proton is both spinning and

591
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:06,320
charged, it behaves like a little

592
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:08,960
current loop. And any current loop

593
00:23:06,320 --> 00:23:11,039
produces a magnetic field.

594
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:13,440
This is why we say a spinning proton has

595
00:23:11,039 --> 00:23:15,600
a magnetic moment. You can picture it as

596
00:23:13,440 --> 00:23:17,840
a miniature bar magnet with a north pole

597
00:23:15,600 --> 00:23:19,919
and a south pole.

598
00:23:17,840 --> 00:23:21,919
If we take just one proton, say from a

599
00:23:19,919 --> 00:23:24,480
hydrogen atom in a water molecule, it

600
00:23:21,919 --> 00:23:26,240
acts like a tiny magnet.

601
00:23:24,480 --> 00:23:27,919
But in the body, we have countless

602
00:23:26,240 --> 00:23:29,919
protons and in the absence of an

603
00:23:27,919 --> 00:23:32,960
external magnetic field, their magnetic

604
00:23:29,919 --> 00:23:35,039
moments point in random directions. As a

605
00:23:32,960 --> 00:23:38,000
result, they cancel out and there is no

606
00:23:35,039 --> 00:23:40,240
overall magnetic effect.

607
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:41,760
However, when we apply a strong external

608
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:44,080
magnetic field, something very

609
00:23:41,760 --> 00:23:45,840
interesting happens. These magnetic

610
00:23:44,080 --> 00:23:48,159
moments begin to align and that

611
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:50,880
alignment is what

612
00:23:48,159 --> 00:23:54,840
MRI relies on generating signals. We

613
00:23:50,880 --> 00:23:54,840
will come to that point soon.

614
00:23:55,200 --> 00:23:59,520
Here we arrive at two key concepts you

615
00:23:57,440 --> 00:24:01,520
must know. Angular momentum usually

616
00:23:59,520 --> 00:24:03,600
written as P and the magnetic moment

617
00:24:01,520 --> 00:24:05,600
written as mu.

618
00:24:03,600 --> 00:24:07,679
From mechanics, angular momentum

619
00:24:05,600 --> 00:24:10,080
describes the rotation of a particle in

620
00:24:07,679 --> 00:24:12,320
this case the proton.

621
00:24:10,080 --> 00:24:14,240
You can think of it as a spinning top.

622
00:24:12,320 --> 00:24:16,400
Just as torque can change the angular

623
00:24:14,240 --> 00:24:18,159
momentum of a top, external influences

624
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:19,919
can change the angular momentum of a

625
00:24:18,159 --> 00:24:21,919
proton.

626
00:24:19,919 --> 00:24:24,720
But unlike a simple spinning top, the

627
00:24:21,919 --> 00:24:26,159
proton also carries an electric charge.

628
00:24:24,720 --> 00:24:27,679
Because of this it has not only

629
00:24:26,159 --> 00:24:30,159
mechanical properties but also

630
00:24:27,679 --> 00:24:32,000
electromagnetic ones. Its magnetic

631
00:24:30,159 --> 00:24:34,000
behavior is summarized by the magnetic

632
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:35,840
moment mu.

633
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:38,640
The beautiful pod is that these two

634
00:24:35,840 --> 00:24:41,120
quantities angular momentum and magnetic

635
00:24:38,640 --> 00:24:43,919
moment are directly linked. The

636
00:24:41,120 --> 00:24:45,440
relationship is mu equals gamma* p where

637
00:24:43,919 --> 00:24:48,159
gamma is a constant called the

638
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:50,559
gyromagnetic ratio.

639
00:24:48,159 --> 00:24:52,640
Quantum mechanics adds one more layer.

640
00:24:50,559 --> 00:24:55,600
Angular momentum cannot take on any

641
00:24:52,640 --> 00:24:57,200
arbitrary value but is quantized. It is

642
00:24:55,600 --> 00:25:00,080
expressed in terms of the spin quantum

643
00:24:57,200 --> 00:25:02,000
number I for a proton I equals 1/2. So

644
00:25:00,080 --> 00:25:03,679
the angular momentum follows a specific

645
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:05,919
formula.

646
00:25:03,679 --> 00:25:07,679
The main takeaway is this. The proton's

647
00:25:05,919 --> 00:25:09,760
mechanical rotation and its

648
00:25:07,679 --> 00:25:11,840
electromagnetic behavior are tied

649
00:25:09,760 --> 00:25:14,320
together in a very simple and elegant

650
00:25:11,840 --> 00:25:17,120
way. This link forms the basis of how

651
00:25:14,320 --> 00:25:20,120
MRI exploits proton spins to generate

652
00:25:17,120 --> 00:25:20,120
signals.

653
00:25:21,679 --> 00:25:25,840
When a proton with a magnetic moment is

654
00:25:23,919 --> 00:25:28,720
placed in a strong external magnetic

655
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:30,480
field, its behavior becomes quantized.

656
00:25:28,720 --> 00:25:32,320
Classically, you might imagine that the

657
00:25:30,480 --> 00:25:34,640
magnetic moment could point in any

658
00:25:32,320 --> 00:25:36,640
direction. But quantum mechanics tells

659
00:25:34,640 --> 00:25:38,559
us that only certain orientations are

660
00:25:36,640 --> 00:25:40,080
allowed.

661
00:25:38,559 --> 00:25:42,240
Specifically, we focus on the

662
00:25:40,080 --> 00:25:44,240
longitudinal component of the magnetic

663
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:46,640
moment, meaning the part aligned with

664
00:25:44,240 --> 00:25:48,640
the external field.

665
00:25:46,640 --> 00:25:51,120
For the proton, this component can take

666
00:25:48,640 --> 00:25:54,080
on only two values. One parallel to the

667
00:25:51,120 --> 00:25:56,320
field and one antiparallel. These values

668
00:25:54,080 --> 00:25:59,279
are determined by the nuclear magnetic

669
00:25:56,320 --> 00:26:02,799
quantum number my which for a proton can

670
00:25:59,279 --> 00:26:04,880
be + 1/2 or minus 1/2.

671
00:26:02,799 --> 00:26:07,840
So the z component of the magnetic

672
00:26:04,880 --> 00:26:11,039
moment muzz equals plus or minus gamma*

673
00:26:07,840 --> 00:26:12,720
plank's constant / 4 pi. This means the

674
00:26:11,039 --> 00:26:15,200
magnetic moment is never perfectly

675
00:26:12,720 --> 00:26:16,880
aligned. It is always tilted slightly.

676
00:26:15,200 --> 00:26:19,120
But it is restricted to these two

677
00:26:16,880 --> 00:26:21,120
possible states.

678
00:26:19,120 --> 00:26:23,360
This quantum restriction, the fact that

679
00:26:21,120 --> 00:26:25,679
the magnetic moment can only take on

680
00:26:23,360 --> 00:26:28,159
discrete orientations, is what gives

681
00:26:25,679 --> 00:26:31,559
rise to the fundamental energy levels we

682
00:26:28,159 --> 00:26:31,559
use in MRI.

683
00:26:33,200 --> 00:26:37,279
When we place spinning protons, each

684
00:26:35,279 --> 00:26:39,200
with a magnetic moment into a strong

685
00:26:37,279 --> 00:26:41,760
external magnetic field, their energy

686
00:26:39,200 --> 00:26:43,919
levels split. This phenomenon is called

687
00:26:41,760 --> 00:26:46,240
the Zemen effect.

688
00:26:43,919 --> 00:26:48,480
The magnetic moment of a proton can only

689
00:26:46,240 --> 00:26:50,880
align in one of two possible ways with

690
00:26:48,480 --> 00:26:53,360
respect to the external field parallel

691
00:26:50,880 --> 00:26:55,120
or antiparallel.

692
00:26:53,360 --> 00:26:56,880
In the parallel case, the magnetic

693
00:26:55,120 --> 00:26:58,960
moment lines up with the field and this

694
00:26:56,880 --> 00:27:00,960
state has lower energy. In the

695
00:26:58,960 --> 00:27:02,559
antiparallel case, the magnetic moment

696
00:27:00,960 --> 00:27:04,960
points against the field and this state

697
00:27:02,559 --> 00:27:06,720
has higher energy.

698
00:27:04,960 --> 00:27:08,480
So instead of a continuous range of

699
00:27:06,720 --> 00:27:10,480
orientations, quantum mechanics

700
00:27:08,480 --> 00:27:12,880
restricts protons to just these two

701
00:27:10,480 --> 00:27:14,480
discrete states. The energy difference

702
00:27:12,880 --> 00:27:17,279
between them is proportional to the

703
00:27:14,480 --> 00:27:19,520
strength of the magnetic field.

704
00:27:17,279 --> 00:27:21,919
This is similar to a mechanical analogy.

705
00:27:19,520 --> 00:27:24,640
Imagine trying to rotate a bar magnet in

706
00:27:21,919 --> 00:27:26,480
a strong external field. If you align it

707
00:27:24,640 --> 00:27:28,640
with the field, that is the stable low

708
00:27:26,480 --> 00:27:30,400
energy position. If you force it to

709
00:27:28,640 --> 00:27:33,520
oppose the field, that requires work and

710
00:27:30,400 --> 00:27:35,120
corresponds to a higher energy state.

711
00:27:33,520 --> 00:27:37,679
This splitting of energy levels is

712
00:27:35,120 --> 00:27:39,360
fundamental in MRI. It is the small

713
00:27:37,679 --> 00:27:41,440
difference in populations between

714
00:27:39,360 --> 00:27:43,840
protons in the lower energy parallel

715
00:27:41,440 --> 00:27:45,279
state and the higher energy antiparallel

716
00:27:43,840 --> 00:27:47,360
state that generates the net

717
00:27:45,279 --> 00:27:50,360
magnetization we rely on to produce

718
00:27:47,360 --> 00:27:50,360
signals.

719
00:27:51,919 --> 00:27:55,840
When protons are placed in a strong

720
00:27:53,760 --> 00:27:58,000
magnetic field they split into two

721
00:27:55,840 --> 00:28:00,159
energy states. The parallel state which

722
00:27:58,000 --> 00:28:02,399
has lower energy and the antiparallel

723
00:28:00,159 --> 00:28:04,799
state which has higher energy. This is

724
00:28:02,399 --> 00:28:06,480
the zemen effect.

725
00:28:04,799 --> 00:28:11,520
The energy of each state can be

726
00:28:06,480 --> 00:28:13,919
expressed as E= Mus * B KN.

727
00:28:11,520 --> 00:28:16,559
Here muzz is the longitudinal component

728
00:28:13,919 --> 00:28:19,120
of the magnetic moment and B KN is the

729
00:28:16,559 --> 00:28:21,600
strength of the external magnetic field.

730
00:28:19,120 --> 00:28:24,960
Because mus can take on two values plus

731
00:28:21,600 --> 00:28:28,480
gamma H over 4 pi or minus gamma H over

732
00:28:24,960 --> 00:28:32,640
4 pi. The energies are E= plus or minus

733
00:28:28,480 --> 00:28:34,159
gamma * H * B KN / 4<unk>.

734
00:28:32,640 --> 00:28:36,559
The difference between these two levels

735
00:28:34,159 --> 00:28:42,399
is what we call delta E and it is given

736
00:28:36,559 --> 00:28:43,919
by delta E= gamma* H * B K / 2 pi.

737
00:28:42,399 --> 00:28:46,320
This difference is critical because it

738
00:28:43,919 --> 00:28:48,080
sets the resonance condition. Only when

739
00:28:46,320 --> 00:28:50,399
the energy of the applied radio

740
00:28:48,080 --> 00:28:54,000
frequency matches this delta E can

741
00:28:50,399 --> 00:28:55,760
protons flip between the two states.

742
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:58,000
At body temperature, slightly more

743
00:28:55,760 --> 00:28:59,600
protons are in the lower energy parallel

744
00:28:58,000 --> 00:29:02,320
state compared to the higher energy

745
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:04,480
antiparallel state. This small imbalance

746
00:29:02,320 --> 00:29:08,440
is what produces the net magnetization

747
00:29:04,480 --> 00:29:08,440
that we detect in MRI.

748
00:29:10,159 --> 00:29:13,840
Now let's bring in some mathematics

749
00:29:11,840 --> 00:29:16,000
through the Boltzman distribution which

750
00:29:13,840 --> 00:29:18,399
describes how protons split between the

751
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:20,480
two energy states.

752
00:29:18,399 --> 00:29:22,720
We can write the ratio of the number of

753
00:29:20,480 --> 00:29:25,520
protons in the antiparallel state to the

754
00:29:22,720 --> 00:29:27,840
number in the parallel state as n

755
00:29:25,520 --> 00:29:29,919
antiparallel divided by n parallel

756
00:29:27,840 --> 00:29:32,399
equals the exponential of negative delta

757
00:29:29,919 --> 00:29:34,399
e over kt.

758
00:29:32,399 --> 00:29:36,000
Here delta e is the energy difference

759
00:29:34,399 --> 00:29:38,720
between the two states. K is the

760
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:41,600
boltzman constant and t is the absolute

761
00:29:38,720 --> 00:29:44,240
temperature in kelvin. Substituting the

762
00:29:41,600 --> 00:29:47,120
expression for delta E, we get n

763
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:53,039
antiparallel / n parallel equals the

764
00:29:47,120 --> 00:29:55,039
exponential of gamma * h * b 0 / 2 pt.

765
00:29:53,039 --> 00:29:58,159
With a first order approximation, this

766
00:29:55,039 --> 00:30:01,279
becomes n antiparallel over n parallel

767
00:29:58,159 --> 00:30:03,840
is approximately equal to 1 - gamma hb 0

768
00:30:01,279 --> 00:30:06,159
/ 2 pi kt.

769
00:30:03,840 --> 00:30:08,159
What does this mean in practice? It

770
00:30:06,159 --> 00:30:10,640
means the populations of the two states

771
00:30:08,159 --> 00:30:14,240
are nearly equal with only a tiny excess

772
00:30:10,640 --> 00:30:16,559
in the parallel or lower energy state.

773
00:30:14,240 --> 00:30:18,880
The net MRI signal comes from this small

774
00:30:16,559 --> 00:30:20,240
population difference. If we take the

775
00:30:18,880 --> 00:30:23,200
difference in numbers between the

776
00:30:20,240 --> 00:30:29,440
parallel and antiparallel states, we get

777
00:30:23,200 --> 00:30:31,600
delta n= ns * gamma hb0 / 4 pi kt.

778
00:30:29,440 --> 00:30:34,000
Here ns is the total number of protons

779
00:30:31,600 --> 00:30:36,799
in the body. The key point is that this

780
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:38,559
difference is extremely small.

781
00:30:36,799 --> 00:30:40,640
For example, at a magnetic field

782
00:30:38,559 --> 00:30:43,279
strength of 1 and a half Tesla, out of

783
00:30:40,640 --> 00:30:46,000
about 1 million protons, only a handful

784
00:30:43,279 --> 00:30:48,080
contribute to the net signal.

785
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:50,080
So although the individual imbalance is

786
00:30:48,080 --> 00:30:52,320
tiny, the collective contribution of

787
00:30:50,080 --> 00:30:56,760
billions and billions of protons is what

788
00:30:52,320 --> 00:30:56,760
makes MRI signals measurable.

789
00:30:58,399 --> 00:31:01,600
Now, all of these models we've

790
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:03,919
discussed, including the Boltzman

791
00:31:01,600 --> 00:31:06,720
distribution, set the stage for the next

792
00:31:03,919 --> 00:31:08,720
key idea, precession.

793
00:31:06,720 --> 00:31:10,720
When a magnetic moment sits inside a

794
00:31:08,720 --> 00:31:12,559
strong external magnetic field, it

795
00:31:10,720 --> 00:31:15,440
doesn't simply align once and stay

796
00:31:12,559 --> 00:31:18,640
fixed. Instead, it underos a motion very

797
00:31:15,440 --> 00:31:20,480
much like a spinning top. The top leans

798
00:31:18,640 --> 00:31:23,039
and slowly wobbles around the vertical

799
00:31:20,480 --> 00:31:24,880
axis. In the same way, the magnetic

800
00:31:23,039 --> 00:31:26,960
moment traces out a procession around

801
00:31:24,880 --> 00:31:29,760
the magnetic field direction. We'll go

802
00:31:26,960 --> 00:31:31,600
into more detail on this soon.

803
00:31:29,760 --> 00:31:33,520
To explain why this happens, we need to

804
00:31:31,600 --> 00:31:35,760
go back to Newton's second law, not just

805
00:31:33,520 --> 00:31:38,399
in the familiar form, force equals mass

806
00:31:35,760 --> 00:31:40,880
time acceleration, but in the rotational

807
00:31:38,399 --> 00:31:43,760
context. In rotations, the central

808
00:31:40,880 --> 00:31:45,360
quantity is angular momentum.

809
00:31:43,760 --> 00:31:47,360
The law tells us that the time

810
00:31:45,360 --> 00:31:50,480
derivative of angular momentum written

811
00:31:47,360 --> 00:31:52,480
as dl over dt is equal to torque. So

812
00:31:50,480 --> 00:31:55,039
torque is the rotational analog of

813
00:31:52,480 --> 00:31:56,799
force. Just as force changes linear

814
00:31:55,039 --> 00:31:58,559
momentum, torque changes angular

815
00:31:56,799 --> 00:32:00,640
momentum.

816
00:31:58,559 --> 00:32:02,880
The derivation on this slide shows the

817
00:32:00,640 --> 00:32:04,720
details. If you're interested in the

818
00:32:02,880 --> 00:32:07,120
full proof, you can follow it step by

819
00:32:04,720 --> 00:32:08,799
step. If not, you can simply trust the

820
00:32:07,120 --> 00:32:11,919
key result. The rate of change of

821
00:32:08,799 --> 00:32:13,360
angular momentum equals torque.

822
00:32:11,919 --> 00:32:18,039
This is the foundation we need to

823
00:32:13,360 --> 00:32:18,039
understand procession in MRI physics.

824
00:32:19,519 --> 00:32:23,760
This is a classic example of procession

825
00:32:22,080 --> 00:32:26,159
and it is the same principle that

826
00:32:23,760 --> 00:32:28,559
applies in MRI when the magnetic moment

827
00:32:26,159 --> 00:32:30,320
of protons precesses in a magnetic

828
00:32:28,559 --> 00:32:32,799
field.

829
00:32:30,320 --> 00:32:34,799
Think of a spinning top. The top's axis

830
00:32:32,799 --> 00:32:37,600
of rotation points in one direction

831
00:32:34,799 --> 00:32:39,840
representing the angular momentum. If no

832
00:32:37,600 --> 00:32:41,919
external force acts on it, the top will

833
00:32:39,840 --> 00:32:45,279
keep spinning steadily just as a moving

834
00:32:41,919 --> 00:32:47,600
object keeps moving in a straight line.

835
00:32:45,279 --> 00:32:49,840
Now if a force is applied here gravity

836
00:32:47,600 --> 00:32:52,080
acting at the center of mass it produces

837
00:32:49,840 --> 00:32:54,399
a torque. Torque is given by the

838
00:32:52,080 --> 00:32:57,279
crossroduct of the lever arm vector R

839
00:32:54,399 --> 00:32:59,600
and the force vector F. In this case R

840
00:32:57,279 --> 00:33:01,200
cross F points into the page. That means

841
00:32:59,600 --> 00:33:03,440
the torque is perpendicular to the

842
00:33:01,200 --> 00:33:05,440
angular momentum.

843
00:33:03,440 --> 00:33:07,279
When the torque is perpendicular, it

844
00:33:05,440 --> 00:33:09,760
doesn't stop the motion or flip the top

845
00:33:07,279 --> 00:33:11,840
over directly. Instead, it causes a

846
00:33:09,760 --> 00:33:14,000
small change delta L that is also

847
00:33:11,840 --> 00:33:16,559
perpendicular to the original angular

848
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:18,799
momentum. This sideways change makes the

849
00:33:16,559 --> 00:33:20,880
tip of the angular momentum vector trace

850
00:33:18,799 --> 00:33:22,880
out a circle.

851
00:33:20,880 --> 00:33:25,200
So instead of falling over the spinning

852
00:33:22,880 --> 00:33:27,200
top precesses, it wobbles around in a

853
00:33:25,200 --> 00:33:29,279
circular path.

854
00:33:27,200 --> 00:33:31,519
And that is the key insight. Whenever a

855
00:33:29,279 --> 00:33:33,519
spinning object with angular momentum

856
00:33:31,519 --> 00:33:36,799
experiences a torque perpendicular to

857
00:33:33,519 --> 00:33:39,200
it, the result is procession.

858
00:33:36,799 --> 00:33:41,279
In MRI, the proton's magnetic moment

859
00:33:39,200 --> 00:33:43,120
behaves just like this spinning top

860
00:33:41,279 --> 00:33:47,159
precessing around the direction of the

861
00:33:43,120 --> 00:33:47,159
external magnetic field.

862
00:33:48,559 --> 00:33:53,200
This idea is not too hard to grasp if we

863
00:33:50,559 --> 00:33:55,039
think about orbital motion.

864
00:33:53,200 --> 00:33:56,799
Take the example of the moon orbiting

865
00:33:55,039 --> 00:33:59,039
around the earth or a satellite orbiting

866
00:33:56,799 --> 00:34:01,360
a planet. You might wonder why doesn't

867
00:33:59,039 --> 00:34:03,200
it just fall straight down? The answer

868
00:34:01,360 --> 00:34:05,360
is that there is always a centripal

869
00:34:03,200 --> 00:34:07,279
force pointing inward toward the center

870
00:34:05,360 --> 00:34:09,200
of the orbit.

871
00:34:07,279 --> 00:34:11,040
That centrial force doesn't change the

872
00:34:09,200 --> 00:34:13,280
magnitude of the velocity, but it does

873
00:34:11,040 --> 00:34:15,520
change its direction. Because the force

874
00:34:13,280 --> 00:34:18,320
is always perpendicular to the velocity

875
00:34:15,520 --> 00:34:20,320
vector, it continuously bends the path,

876
00:34:18,320 --> 00:34:22,159
keeping the satellite in circular motion

877
00:34:20,320 --> 00:34:24,159
rather than letting it fly off in a

878
00:34:22,159 --> 00:34:26,399
straight line.

879
00:34:24,159 --> 00:34:29,200
Mathematically the centrial force is

880
00:34:26,399 --> 00:34:34,000
equal to mass time velocity squared

881
00:34:29,200 --> 00:34:36,240
divided by the radius F= mv^2 / r.

882
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:38,079
Now connect this to angular momentum.

883
00:34:36,240 --> 00:34:40,320
When the change in a vector is always

884
00:34:38,079 --> 00:34:43,200
perpendicular to the vector itself, the

885
00:34:40,320 --> 00:34:45,599
result is circular motion.

886
00:34:43,200 --> 00:34:47,839
In the orbital case, the velocity vector

887
00:34:45,599 --> 00:34:50,159
keeps changing direction. While in

888
00:34:47,839 --> 00:34:52,879
angular momentum, the same principle

889
00:34:50,159 --> 00:34:55,359
applies. Torque causes a perpendicular

890
00:34:52,879 --> 00:34:57,599
change in angular momentum and so the

891
00:34:55,359 --> 00:34:59,680
angular momentum vector itself traces

892
00:34:57,599 --> 00:35:01,359
out a circle.

893
00:34:59,680 --> 00:35:03,839
This is the key point to understand

894
00:35:01,359 --> 00:35:07,560
procession. A perpendicular change leads

895
00:35:03,839 --> 00:35:07,560
to circular motion.

896
00:35:09,200 --> 00:35:12,960
When a magnetic moment is placed in an

897
00:35:10,960 --> 00:35:15,599
external magnetic field, it experiences

898
00:35:12,960 --> 00:35:17,440
a torque. This torque does not flip the

899
00:35:15,599 --> 00:35:19,520
magnetic moment directly into alignment

900
00:35:17,440 --> 00:35:21,440
with the field.

901
00:35:19,520 --> 00:35:24,000
Instead, it causes the moment to

902
00:35:21,440 --> 00:35:26,320
precess, meaning it rotates around the

903
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:28,480
axis of the magnetic field, very much

904
00:35:26,320 --> 00:35:30,560
like a spinning top under the influence

905
00:35:28,480 --> 00:35:32,160
of gravity.

906
00:35:30,560 --> 00:35:34,720
The rate of this procession is called

907
00:35:32,160 --> 00:35:36,560
the Larmore frequency. The Lmore

908
00:35:34,720 --> 00:35:38,400
frequency depends on two things. The

909
00:35:36,560 --> 00:35:41,200
strength of the magnetic field and a

910
00:35:38,400 --> 00:35:42,960
constant called the gyromagnetic ratio,

911
00:35:41,200 --> 00:35:44,960
which is unique for each type of

912
00:35:42,960 --> 00:35:46,720
nucleus.

913
00:35:44,960 --> 00:35:50,320
Mathematically we write the lore

914
00:35:46,720 --> 00:35:52,800
frequency as omega 0 equals gamma * b 0.

915
00:35:50,320 --> 00:35:55,119
Here omega 0 represents the procession

916
00:35:52,800 --> 00:35:57,280
frequency, gamma is the gyromagnetic

917
00:35:55,119 --> 00:35:59,520
ratio and b 0 is the strength of the

918
00:35:57,280 --> 00:36:01,359
magnetic field.

919
00:35:59,520 --> 00:36:03,119
This relationship tells us that the

920
00:36:01,359 --> 00:36:05,200
stronger the field, the faster the

921
00:36:03,119 --> 00:36:07,440
procession. And this procession

922
00:36:05,200 --> 00:36:09,359
frequency is the key to MRI because it

923
00:36:07,440 --> 00:36:12,079
sets the frequency at which protons

924
00:36:09,359 --> 00:36:17,000
respond to radio frequency pulses and

925
00:36:12,079 --> 00:36:17,000
generate the measurable MRI signal.

926
00:36:18,480 --> 00:36:23,280
Now let's carefully look at how we can

927
00:36:20,240 --> 00:36:25,839
compute the precessional frequency.

928
00:36:23,280 --> 00:36:27,839
When a magnetic moment which we call mu

929
00:36:25,839 --> 00:36:30,160
is placed at an angle to the external

930
00:36:27,839 --> 00:36:32,720
magnetic field B, it experiences a

931
00:36:30,160 --> 00:36:35,680
torque. This torque can be written as mu

932
00:36:32,720 --> 00:36:39,280
crossb 0. That torque is what drives the

933
00:36:35,680 --> 00:36:41,599
angular momentum to change over time.

934
00:36:39,280 --> 00:36:43,839
Mathematically we can say torque equals

935
00:36:41,599 --> 00:36:46,480
the derivative of angular momentum with

936
00:36:43,839 --> 00:36:49,359
respect to time. In other words, dp by

937
00:36:46,480 --> 00:36:52,240
dt= mu cross b 0.

938
00:36:49,359 --> 00:36:54,480
Here p is the angular momentum. Because

939
00:36:52,240 --> 00:36:56,720
protons both have mass and positive

940
00:36:54,480 --> 00:36:59,040
charge, their spinning motion not only

941
00:36:56,720 --> 00:37:02,079
produces angular momentum, but also

942
00:36:59,040 --> 00:37:04,160
generates a tiny current loop.

943
00:37:02,079 --> 00:37:06,560
That current loop is associated with a

944
00:37:04,160 --> 00:37:08,480
magnetic moment. And so whenever the

945
00:37:06,560 --> 00:37:11,680
magnetic moment is not aligned with the

946
00:37:08,480 --> 00:37:13,599
magnetic field, it feels a torque.

947
00:37:11,680 --> 00:37:15,760
Now to connect the pieces, magnetic

948
00:37:13,599 --> 00:37:17,839
moment and angular momentum are directly

949
00:37:15,760 --> 00:37:19,760
proportional. That means the change in

950
00:37:17,839 --> 00:37:22,240
angular momentum is tied to the change

951
00:37:19,760 --> 00:37:23,920
in magnetic moment.

952
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:25,920
To see how this becomes precision,

953
00:37:23,920 --> 00:37:28,320
consider a very small angular change

954
00:37:25,920 --> 00:37:30,160
which we call d5. For such small

955
00:37:28,320 --> 00:37:32,960
changes, the sign of d5 can be

956
00:37:30,160 --> 00:37:34,800
approximated as just d5. With this, we

957
00:37:32,960 --> 00:37:37,440
can relate torque to the rate of change

958
00:37:34,800 --> 00:37:39,599
of the angular position.

959
00:37:37,440 --> 00:37:42,240
So the angular frequency of procession

960
00:37:39,599 --> 00:37:44,240
written as omega is equal to the torque

961
00:37:42,240 --> 00:37:47,280
divided by the magnitude of angular

962
00:37:44,240 --> 00:37:48,720
momentum time sin theta. If you expand

963
00:37:47,280 --> 00:37:52,720
the cross productduct, you eventually

964
00:37:48,720 --> 00:37:55,200
find that omega equals gamma* b 0.

965
00:37:52,720 --> 00:37:58,400
Here gamma is the gyromagnetic ratio, a

966
00:37:55,200 --> 00:38:00,160
constant specific to the nucleus.

967
00:37:58,400 --> 00:38:02,560
This final result is extremely

968
00:38:00,160 --> 00:38:04,480
important. The processional frequency is

969
00:38:02,560 --> 00:38:06,880
directly proportional to the strength of

970
00:38:04,480 --> 00:38:09,359
the magnetic field. In a stronger field,

971
00:38:06,880 --> 00:38:11,680
the spins process faster. In a weaker

972
00:38:09,359 --> 00:38:13,440
field, they process more slowly. This

973
00:38:11,680 --> 00:38:17,000
proportionality is the foundation of

974
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:17,000
magnetic resonance.

975
00:38:18,560 --> 00:38:22,240
It's often much easier to demonstrate

976
00:38:20,640 --> 00:38:25,440
precision than to explain it with

977
00:38:22,240 --> 00:38:27,280
equations. Here you see a gyroscope. Its

978
00:38:25,440 --> 00:38:29,760
circular motion around the stand is

979
00:38:27,280 --> 00:38:31,920
precession. This motion results from the

980
00:38:29,760 --> 00:38:33,599
combination of two effects. The downward

981
00:38:31,920 --> 00:38:36,800
force of gravity and the angular

982
00:38:33,599 --> 00:38:38,480
momentum around the spinning axis.

983
00:38:36,800 --> 00:38:41,200
Notice how the wheel does not simply

984
00:38:38,480 --> 00:38:42,720
fall. Instead, because of torque, it

985
00:38:41,200 --> 00:38:45,280
turns around the point where it is

986
00:38:42,720 --> 00:38:47,359
supported. If I increase the downward

987
00:38:45,280 --> 00:38:49,599
force, for example, by adding the weight

988
00:38:47,359 --> 00:38:53,359
of a wrench to the axle, you can see

989
00:38:49,599 --> 00:38:55,119
that the procession frequency increases.

990
00:38:53,359 --> 00:38:58,000
This is the same principle that applies

991
00:38:55,119 --> 00:38:59,680
in MRI. The frequency of procession is

992
00:38:58,000 --> 00:39:02,240
directly linked to the strength of the

993
00:38:59,680 --> 00:39:04,560
magnetic field. Stronger forces or

994
00:39:02,240 --> 00:39:06,640
fields lead to faster procession. We

995
00:39:04,560 --> 00:39:09,040
call this frequency encoding and it is

996
00:39:06,640 --> 00:39:12,520
the foundation for how MRI gathers

997
00:39:09,040 --> 00:39:12,520
spatial information.

998
00:39:14,240 --> 00:39:19,200
Now we move from individual protons to

999
00:39:16,320 --> 00:39:21,280
the idea of magnetization.

1000
00:39:19,200 --> 00:39:23,040
Each proton carries a magnetic moment

1001
00:39:21,280 --> 00:39:25,040
and as we have discussed these moments

1002
00:39:23,040 --> 00:39:26,640
precess around the external magnetic

1003
00:39:25,040 --> 00:39:28,720
field.

1004
00:39:26,640 --> 00:39:30,800
In the population of protons slightly

1005
00:39:28,720 --> 00:39:33,200
more occupy the lower energy state

1006
00:39:30,800 --> 00:39:35,119
aligned parallel to the magnetic field

1007
00:39:33,200 --> 00:39:37,440
while slightly fewer are in the higher

1008
00:39:35,119 --> 00:39:39,440
energy antiparallel state. This

1009
00:39:37,440 --> 00:39:41,200
imbalance, even though very small, is

1010
00:39:39,440 --> 00:39:42,720
crucial

1011
00:39:41,200 --> 00:39:44,800
because the magnetic moments are

1012
00:39:42,720 --> 00:39:46,800
vectors. Those that are opposite to each

1013
00:39:44,800 --> 00:39:48,560
other will cancel out in the transverse

1014
00:39:46,800 --> 00:39:50,480
plane.

1015
00:39:48,560 --> 00:39:52,640
What remains is a small excess of

1016
00:39:50,480 --> 00:39:54,720
protons in the parallel state. And when

1017
00:39:52,640 --> 00:39:56,640
we add up all of their contributions, we

1018
00:39:54,720 --> 00:39:58,400
obtain a single net vector pointing

1019
00:39:56,640 --> 00:40:00,400
along the direction of the magnetic

1020
00:39:58,400 --> 00:40:02,880
field. This is what we call the net

1021
00:40:00,400 --> 00:40:04,560
magnetization vector, often denoted as

1022
00:40:02,880 --> 00:40:06,320
M.

1023
00:40:04,560 --> 00:40:07,920
From this point on, instead of worrying

1024
00:40:06,320 --> 00:40:10,160
about the behavior of individual

1025
00:40:07,920 --> 00:40:12,720
protons, we can focus on this collective

1026
00:40:10,160 --> 00:40:14,640
magnetization vector.

1027
00:40:12,720 --> 00:40:16,960
We can treat it as a classical vector

1028
00:40:14,640 --> 00:40:19,280
that can tilt, rotate or precess just

1029
00:40:16,960 --> 00:40:21,040
like a spinning top. This makes it much

1030
00:40:19,280 --> 00:40:24,240
easier to understand the physics and to

1031
00:40:21,040 --> 00:40:26,400
design MRI pulse sequences.

1032
00:40:24,240 --> 00:40:28,400
So, magnetization is the bridge from the

1033
00:40:26,400 --> 00:40:33,079
microscopic quantum world of spins to

1034
00:40:28,400 --> 00:40:33,079
the macroscopic signals we use in MRI.

1035
00:40:34,720 --> 00:40:37,599
Now we bring everything together and

1036
00:40:36,320 --> 00:40:40,000
look at the steady state of

1037
00:40:37,599 --> 00:40:42,240
magnetization.

1038
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:44,800
Earlier we talked about the tiny surplus

1039
00:40:42,240 --> 00:40:46,800
of protons in the lower energy parallel

1040
00:40:44,800 --> 00:40:49,440
state compared with those in the higher

1041
00:40:46,800 --> 00:40:51,280
energy antiparallel state. That

1042
00:40:49,440 --> 00:40:53,200
difference is very small but when

1043
00:40:51,280 --> 00:40:55,839
multiplied by the enormous total number

1044
00:40:53,200 --> 00:40:57,920
of protons in the body it adds up to a

1045
00:40:55,839 --> 00:41:00,000
measurable effect.

1046
00:40:57,920 --> 00:41:03,200
For a single proton, the magnetic moment

1047
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:05,599
can be expressed as gamma * h bar / 2.

1048
00:41:03,200 --> 00:41:08,880
But now instead of just one proton, we

1049
00:41:05,599 --> 00:41:10,880
have on the order of 10 ^ of 23 protons.

1050
00:41:08,880 --> 00:41:13,440
And only a small fraction contributes to

1051
00:41:10,880 --> 00:41:15,280
the net imbalance.

1052
00:41:13,440 --> 00:41:17,119
Multiplying that tiny difference by the

1053
00:41:15,280 --> 00:41:19,359
large population gives us the bulk

1054
00:41:17,119 --> 00:41:22,560
magnetization.

1055
00:41:19,359 --> 00:41:24,319
We call this net magnetization m. It

1056
00:41:22,560 --> 00:41:26,400
represents the collective contribution

1057
00:41:24,319 --> 00:41:30,079
of all the protons and points along the

1058
00:41:26,400 --> 00:41:32,079
direction of the external field B KN.

1059
00:41:30,079 --> 00:41:34,480
In this steady state, the magnetization

1060
00:41:32,079 --> 00:41:36,560
only has a longitudinal component. That

1061
00:41:34,480 --> 00:41:38,880
means MZ equals M KN. While the

1062
00:41:36,560 --> 00:41:40,640
transverse components MX and MY are both

1063
00:41:38,880 --> 00:41:42,640
zero.

1064
00:41:40,640 --> 00:41:44,800
Even though individual protons are still

1065
00:41:42,640 --> 00:41:47,280
processing and flipping between parallel

1066
00:41:44,800 --> 00:41:49,119
and antiparallel orientations, when you

1067
00:41:47,280 --> 00:41:52,000
take the average, the only surviving

1068
00:41:49,119 --> 00:41:53,760
component is along the Z-axis. This is

1069
00:41:52,000 --> 00:41:56,760
what we refer to as the steady state

1070
00:41:53,760 --> 00:41:56,760
magnetization.

1071
00:41:58,880 --> 00:42:03,280
So far, we've spent quite some time on

1072
00:42:00,800 --> 00:42:04,960
the physical foundation.

1073
00:42:03,280 --> 00:42:07,599
That's good because now you have a solid

1074
00:42:04,960 --> 00:42:09,839
grounding in the physics behind MRI,

1075
00:42:07,599 --> 00:42:12,240
angular momentum, magnetic moment,

1076
00:42:09,839 --> 00:42:14,000
procession, and magnetization.

1077
00:42:12,240 --> 00:42:16,000
All of this is essential because without

1078
00:42:14,000 --> 00:42:18,160
that base, the next steps would be very

1079
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:19,920
difficult to follow.

1080
00:42:18,160 --> 00:42:21,839
Now we're ready to move forward and talk

1081
00:42:19,920 --> 00:42:24,400
about how the MRI signal is actually

1082
00:42:21,839 --> 00:42:27,280
generated. This is the transition point

1083
00:42:24,400 --> 00:42:29,040
from theory into application.

1084
00:42:27,280 --> 00:42:31,280
The key question becomes once the

1085
00:42:29,040 --> 00:42:33,520
protons are aligned and processed in the

1086
00:42:31,280 --> 00:42:35,839
magnetic field, how do we disturb them

1087
00:42:33,520 --> 00:42:38,640
in a controlled way and measure the

1088
00:42:35,839 --> 00:42:40,400
response?

1089
00:42:38,640 --> 00:42:43,040
That's where the radio frequency pulse

1090
00:42:40,400 --> 00:42:44,880
comes in. By applying a carefully tuned

1091
00:42:43,040 --> 00:42:47,119
RF pulse, we can perturb the

1092
00:42:44,880 --> 00:42:49,359
magnetization vector and create a

1093
00:42:47,119 --> 00:42:51,359
