If you just leave M alone in its steady

1112
00:43:32,960 --> 00:43:37,680
state, it aligns with the main magnetic

1113
00:43:35,119 --> 00:43:39,839
field and stays constant in time. A

1114
00:43:37,680 --> 00:43:42,880
static field like this will not generate

1115
00:43:39,839 --> 00:43:45,040
any measurable electrical signal.

1116
00:43:42,880 --> 00:43:46,720
Remember, electromagnetic induction only

1117
00:43:45,040 --> 00:43:49,040
works when the magnetic field is

1118
00:43:46,720 --> 00:43:52,240
changing. A constant magnetization

1119
00:43:49,040 --> 00:43:54,960
produces nothing in our detection coil.

1120
00:43:52,240 --> 00:43:56,720
The key idea is this. If we can flip m

1121
00:43:54,960 --> 00:43:58,560
away from its alignment with the main

1122
00:43:56,720 --> 00:44:01,119
field, then it will gain a transverse

1123
00:43:58,560 --> 00:44:03,440
component. That transverse part does not

1124
00:44:01,119 --> 00:44:05,359
just sit there. It precesses, meaning it

1125
00:44:03,440 --> 00:44:07,520
rotates around the axis of the main

1126
00:44:05,359 --> 00:44:09,760
magnetic field.

1127
00:44:07,520 --> 00:44:12,319
This rotating transverse magnetization

1128
00:44:09,760 --> 00:44:14,640
produces an alternating magnetic field.

1129
00:44:12,319 --> 00:44:16,800
An alternating field is exactly what we

1130
00:44:14,640 --> 00:44:19,760
need because it induces an electrical

1131
00:44:16,800 --> 00:44:21,359
signal in the detection coil.

1132
00:44:19,760 --> 00:44:23,839
This was the breakthrough that launched

1133
00:44:21,359 --> 00:44:26,880
nuclear magnetic resonance. It was

1134
00:44:23,839 --> 00:44:29,520
discovered in 1946 by Felix Block at

1135
00:44:26,880 --> 00:44:31,520
Stanford and Edward Pcell at Harvard and

1136
00:44:29,520 --> 00:44:34,960
their work was recognized with the Nobel

1137
00:44:31,520 --> 00:44:37,599
Prize in physics in 1952.

1138
00:44:34,960 --> 00:44:39,920
So the essential trick is flip the net

1139
00:44:37,599 --> 00:44:42,560
magnetization, create a transverse

1140
00:44:39,920 --> 00:44:44,960
component, let it precess and detect the

1141
00:44:42,560 --> 00:44:46,800
alternating signal that comes out. This

1142
00:44:44,960 --> 00:44:49,800
is the foundation of MRI signal

1143
00:44:46,800 --> 00:44:49,800
generation.

1144
00:44:51,440 --> 00:44:55,760
When the magnetization vector is in

1145
00:44:53,440 --> 00:44:57,760
steady state, it is balanced. No

1146
00:44:55,760 --> 00:45:00,240
magnetic field is changing. So no signal

1147
00:44:57,760 --> 00:45:02,480
can be detected. But once we flip it, we

1148
00:45:00,240 --> 00:45:05,680
break that balance. Now there is a

1149
00:45:02,480 --> 00:45:07,359
transverse component of magnetization.

1150
00:45:05,680 --> 00:45:09,119
This transverse part does not stay

1151
00:45:07,359 --> 00:45:11,280
still. It under goes circular motion

1152
00:45:09,119 --> 00:45:13,520
what we call precession. And this

1153
00:45:11,280 --> 00:45:15,920
precessing transverse component produces

1154
00:45:13,520 --> 00:45:18,160
an alternating magnetic field which can

1155
00:45:15,920 --> 00:45:20,319
then be measured through electromagnetic

1156
00:45:18,160 --> 00:45:22,160
induction as described by Maxwell's

1157
00:45:20,319 --> 00:45:24,079
equations.

1158
00:45:22,160 --> 00:45:26,160
So how do we flip the magnetization to

1159
00:45:24,079 --> 00:45:28,160
break the balance?

1160
00:45:26,160 --> 00:45:29,920
To answer that we look at the energy

1161
00:45:28,160 --> 00:45:31,839
difference between the parallel state

1162
00:45:29,920 --> 00:45:34,240
and the antiparallel state of the

1163
00:45:31,839 --> 00:45:37,200
protons. Earlier we derived this

1164
00:45:34,240 --> 00:45:38,960
difference and called it delta E.

1165
00:45:37,200 --> 00:45:41,599
This energy difference must be supplied

1166
00:45:38,960 --> 00:45:43,599
by an incoming electromagnetic wave. And

1167
00:45:41,599 --> 00:45:47,200
the energy carried by a photon is equal

1168
00:45:43,599 --> 00:45:48,960
to plank's constant times the frequency.

1169
00:45:47,200 --> 00:45:51,040
That means the frequency of the applied

1170
00:45:48,960 --> 00:45:52,880
radio frequency wave has to exactly

1171
00:45:51,040 --> 00:45:54,960
match the energy gap between the two

1172
00:45:52,880 --> 00:45:57,040
spin states.

1173
00:45:54,960 --> 00:45:58,880
When you rearrange the formulas, you

1174
00:45:57,040 --> 00:46:03,359
find that the resonant frequency written

1175
00:45:58,880 --> 00:46:05,440
as f is equal to gamma * b 0 / 2<unk>i.

1176
00:46:03,359 --> 00:46:10,079
In terms of angular frequency written as

1177
00:46:05,440 --> 00:46:12,480
omega, the result is omega= gamma * b 0.

1178
00:46:10,079 --> 00:46:14,800
This is a fundamental result. It tells

1179
00:46:12,480 --> 00:46:17,040
us that the lour procession frequency of

1180
00:46:14,800 --> 00:46:19,119
the proton is identical to the frequency

1181
00:46:17,040 --> 00:46:21,520
of the radio frequency field we must

1182
00:46:19,119 --> 00:46:24,960
apply to drive transitions between the

1183
00:46:21,520 --> 00:46:27,280
parallel and the antiparallel states.

1184
00:46:24,960 --> 00:46:29,359
So from the quantum mechanical point of

1185
00:46:27,280 --> 00:46:31,599
view, resonance occurs when the radio

1186
00:46:29,359 --> 00:46:34,319
frequency wave carries exactly the right

1187
00:46:31,599 --> 00:46:39,319
energy to match that gap. And that is

1188
00:46:34,319 --> 00:46:39,319
the basis of nuclear magnetic resonance.

1189
00:46:40,880 --> 00:46:46,000
We can now look at RF excitation from

1190
00:46:42,960 --> 00:46:47,839
the quantum mechanical point of view.

1191
00:46:46,000 --> 00:46:49,839
Imagine we have two energy levels, a

1192
00:46:47,839 --> 00:46:52,400
lower energy state and a higher energy

1193
00:46:49,839 --> 00:46:54,160
state. When we send in a radio frequency

1194
00:46:52,400 --> 00:46:55,760
wave at the resonance frequency, that

1195
00:46:54,160 --> 00:46:57,680
wave carries just the right amount of

1196
00:46:55,760 --> 00:47:00,800
energy to promote a proton from the

1197
00:46:57,680 --> 00:47:03,280
lower state up to the higher state.

1198
00:47:00,800 --> 00:47:05,040
But once the RF exitation stops, those

1199
00:47:03,280 --> 00:47:06,960
protons in the higher energy state

1200
00:47:05,040 --> 00:47:08,800
cannot stay there forever. They

1201
00:47:06,960 --> 00:47:10,720
naturally relax back down to the lower

1202
00:47:08,800 --> 00:47:12,800
energy state, which is the more stable

1203
00:47:10,720 --> 00:47:14,720
configuration.

1204
00:47:12,800 --> 00:47:16,880
As they do so, the excess energy is

1205
00:47:14,720 --> 00:47:19,200
released. Importantly, the released

1206
00:47:16,880 --> 00:47:21,520
energy is in the form of the same radio

1207
00:47:19,200 --> 00:47:23,040
frequency signal that was used to excite

1208
00:47:21,520 --> 00:47:25,040
them.

1209
00:47:23,040 --> 00:47:27,520
This emitted signal is what we detect

1210
00:47:25,040 --> 00:47:29,599
externally. It is the key step that

1211
00:47:27,520 --> 00:47:32,000
allows us to convert the microscopic

1212
00:47:29,599 --> 00:47:37,400
spin transitions of hydrogen protons

1213
00:47:32,000 --> 00:47:37,400
into a measurable macroscopic MR signal.

1214
00:47:38,800 --> 00:47:43,280
Now let's look at the classical view of

1215
00:47:40,640 --> 00:47:45,280
RF excitation. We have our net

1216
00:47:43,280 --> 00:47:47,119
magnetization vector which represents

1217
00:47:45,280 --> 00:47:49,920
the collective magnetic moment of all

1218
00:47:47,119 --> 00:47:52,160
protons in the steady state. This vector

1219
00:47:49,920 --> 00:47:55,280
points along the z-axis aligned with the

1220
00:47:52,160 --> 00:47:57,280
static magnetic field B 0.

1221
00:47:55,280 --> 00:48:00,160
When we apply an additional magnetic

1222
00:47:57,280 --> 00:48:02,720
field called B1 along the X-axis,

1223
00:48:00,160 --> 00:48:04,160
something interesting happens.

1224
00:48:02,720 --> 00:48:06,800
The cross productduct between the

1225
00:48:04,160 --> 00:48:08,880
magnetization vector and B1 produces a

1226
00:48:06,800 --> 00:48:10,880
torque. This torque acts in the

1227
00:48:08,880 --> 00:48:13,040
direction perpendicular to both vectors

1228
00:48:10,880 --> 00:48:15,680
and it causes the magnetization to tip

1229
00:48:13,040 --> 00:48:17,200
away from the Z-axis.

1230
00:48:15,680 --> 00:48:19,040
But remember, the system is still

1231
00:48:17,200 --> 00:48:21,280
progressing around the main magnetic

1232
00:48:19,040 --> 00:48:23,520
field. So, the magnetization doesn't

1233
00:48:21,280 --> 00:48:25,599
simply tilt once and stop. It spirals

1234
00:48:23,520 --> 00:48:28,559
away from the Z-axis, tracing out a

1235
00:48:25,599 --> 00:48:30,559
cone. The longer we apply the B1 field,

1236
00:48:28,559 --> 00:48:32,720
the further the vector tips, increasing

1237
00:48:30,559 --> 00:48:34,480
the flip angle.

1238
00:48:32,720 --> 00:48:36,559
This picture is very convenient to

1239
00:48:34,480 --> 00:48:39,280
describe using the concept of a rotating

1240
00:48:36,559 --> 00:48:41,440
frame. In that frame, the B1 field looks

1241
00:48:39,280 --> 00:48:43,680
stationary and the magnetization vector

1242
00:48:41,440 --> 00:48:46,000
simply rotates around it. That's why we

1243
00:48:43,680 --> 00:48:48,319
often describe RF excitation as flipping

1244
00:48:46,000 --> 00:48:51,319
the magnetization into the transverse

1245
00:48:48,319 --> 00:48:51,319
plane.

1246
00:48:52,640 --> 00:48:56,400
In the laboratory frame, the

1247
00:48:54,160 --> 00:48:59,599
magnetization vector doesn't just tip

1248
00:48:56,400 --> 00:49:01,920
smoothly into the transverse plane.

1249
00:48:59,599 --> 00:49:03,920
Instead, it traces out a spiral path

1250
00:49:01,920 --> 00:49:06,400
because while it is flipping down, it is

1251
00:49:03,920 --> 00:49:09,119
also precessing around the z-axis at the

1252
00:49:06,400 --> 00:49:11,920
lore frequency. So, what we observe

1253
00:49:09,119 --> 00:49:13,760
looks like a helical trajectory.

1254
00:49:11,920 --> 00:49:16,160
But there is a much simpler way to

1255
00:49:13,760 --> 00:49:18,480
describe this motion. Instead of staying

1256
00:49:16,160 --> 00:49:20,480
in the laboratory coordinate system, we

1257
00:49:18,480 --> 00:49:22,720
can shift into a rotating frame of

1258
00:49:20,480 --> 00:49:24,800
reference. This is a coordinate system

1259
00:49:22,720 --> 00:49:26,559
that rotates at exactly the lore

1260
00:49:24,800 --> 00:49:28,480
frequency.

1261
00:49:26,559 --> 00:49:30,960
In this rotating frame, the spiral

1262
00:49:28,480 --> 00:49:33,040
disappears. The magnetization no longer

1263
00:49:30,960 --> 00:49:35,520
seems to precess. It simply tilts or

1264
00:49:33,040 --> 00:49:37,839
flips into the transverse plane. This

1265
00:49:35,520 --> 00:49:40,319
makes the description of RF excitation

1266
00:49:37,839 --> 00:49:42,400
much more intuitive.

1267
00:49:40,319 --> 00:49:44,240
That's why throughout MRI physics, we

1268
00:49:42,400 --> 00:49:46,480
often switch between the laboratory

1269
00:49:44,240 --> 00:49:48,800
frame and the rotating frame. The

1270
00:49:46,480 --> 00:49:50,640
physics is the same, but in the rotating

1271
00:49:48,800 --> 00:49:55,160
frame, the mathematics and the

1272
00:49:50,640 --> 00:49:55,160
visualization become much simpler.

1273
00:49:56,640 --> 00:50:00,880
Think about this in terms of a revolving

1274
00:49:58,640 --> 00:50:02,800
door. If you just walk up and push the

1275
00:50:00,880 --> 00:50:05,119
door randomly, sometimes your push helps

1276
00:50:02,800 --> 00:50:07,040
it move and sometimes it cancels out

1277
00:50:05,119 --> 00:50:09,200
because your force is not always aligned

1278
00:50:07,040 --> 00:50:11,119
in the right way.

1279
00:50:09,200 --> 00:50:13,040
But if you keep pushing at exactly the

1280
00:50:11,119 --> 00:50:15,119
right rhythm, always perpendicular to

1281
00:50:13,040 --> 00:50:17,440
the door, you will steadily drive it

1282
00:50:15,119 --> 00:50:19,520
around in a smooth motion. That is

1283
00:50:17,440 --> 00:50:23,119
resonance. Applying a force at the right

1284
00:50:19,520 --> 00:50:26,240
frequency so that every push adds up. In

1285
00:50:23,119 --> 00:50:27,920
MRI, the same idea holds. The RF signal

1286
00:50:26,240 --> 00:50:29,920
has to be applied at the exact

1287
00:50:27,920 --> 00:50:32,240
processional frequency, the LRmore

1288
00:50:29,920 --> 00:50:34,319
frequency. If it matches, then every

1289
00:50:32,240 --> 00:50:36,960
cycle of the RF field keeps nudging the

1290
00:50:34,319 --> 00:50:38,880
spins in the same direction.

1291
00:50:36,960 --> 00:50:41,280
In the rotating frame, this no longer

1292
00:50:38,880 --> 00:50:43,119
looks like an oscillating wave. Instead,

1293
00:50:41,280 --> 00:50:45,200
it looks like a steady force, a constant

1294
00:50:43,119 --> 00:50:46,960
torque applied to the magnetization

1295
00:50:45,200 --> 00:50:48,640
vector.

1296
00:50:46,960 --> 00:50:51,280
That constant torque is what tips the

1297
00:50:48,640 --> 00:50:53,280
magnetization away from the Z-axis. It

1298
00:50:51,280 --> 00:50:55,280
is what allows us to rotate the vector

1299
00:50:53,280 --> 00:50:58,480
from its equilibrium position into the

1300
00:50:55,280 --> 00:51:00,720
transverse plane or even further.

1301
00:50:58,480 --> 00:51:02,880
So the revolving door is a nice analogy.

1302
00:51:00,720 --> 00:51:05,280
Push in rhythm with the rotation and the

1303
00:51:02,880 --> 00:51:09,559
system responds strongly. Push out of

1304
00:51:05,280 --> 00:51:09,559
rhythm and the effect cancels out.

1305
00:51:10,960 --> 00:51:15,200
We describe the change of the

1306
00:51:12,319 --> 00:51:17,680
magnetization vector m of t with time.

1307
00:51:15,200 --> 00:51:22,000
The block equation is

1308
00:51:17,680 --> 00:51:25,040
dm of t / dt = m of t cross gamma * b of

1309
00:51:22,000 --> 00:51:27,040
t minus r * the difference of m of t and

1310
00:51:25,040 --> 00:51:30,640
m0.

1311
00:51:27,040 --> 00:51:33,680
Here gamma is the gyromagnetic ratio. B

1312
00:51:30,640 --> 00:51:36,640
of t is the magnetic field. M0 is the

1313
00:51:33,680 --> 00:51:39,200
equilibrium magnetization and r is the

1314
00:51:36,640 --> 00:51:42,640
relaxation operator that encodes t1 and

1315
00:51:39,200 --> 00:51:44,880
t2 processes.

1316
00:51:42,640 --> 00:51:48,319
Now if we expand this into components we

1317
00:51:44,880 --> 00:51:51,839
get three equations for the Z component.

1318
00:51:48,319 --> 00:51:55,839
DMZ over DT= gamma* the quantity MX * B

1319
00:51:51,839 --> 00:51:58,160
Y - M * BX minus the difference MZ - M0

1320
00:51:55,839 --> 00:52:02,319
/ T1

1321
00:51:58,160 --> 00:52:07,359
for the X component. dmx over dt = gamma

1322
00:52:02,319 --> 00:52:09,760
* the quant my * bz minus mz * b y - mx

1323
00:52:07,359 --> 00:52:13,200
/ t2

1324
00:52:09,760 --> 00:52:17,599
for the y component. DM my over dt =

1325
00:52:13,200 --> 00:52:22,040
gamma * the quant mz * bx - mx * bz

1326
00:52:17,599 --> 00:52:22,040
minus my / t2.

1327
00:52:23,760 --> 00:52:27,760
Now let's see how the block equation

1328
00:52:25,520 --> 00:52:29,920
works in practice.

1329
00:52:27,760 --> 00:52:32,319
First consider procession. If the

1330
00:52:29,920 --> 00:52:34,480
magnetization vector capital M is not

1331
00:52:32,319 --> 00:52:37,119
parallel to the magnetic field B, then M

1332
00:52:34,480 --> 00:52:38,880
will precess around B.

1333
00:52:37,119 --> 00:52:40,800
On the other hand, if M is perfectly

1334
00:52:38,880 --> 00:52:43,520
parallel to B, then the procession

1335
00:52:40,800 --> 00:52:45,520
radius is zero. In that case, you do not

1336
00:52:43,520 --> 00:52:47,680
see any visible procession even though

1337
00:52:45,520 --> 00:52:50,240
the vector is still technically circling

1338
00:52:47,680 --> 00:52:51,920
like a single dot.

1339
00:52:50,240 --> 00:52:54,640
Next, think about what happens when we

1340
00:52:51,920 --> 00:52:57,200
flip M. Suppose M is rotated away from

1341
00:52:54,640 --> 00:52:59,280
the Z-axis into the transverse plane.

1342
00:52:57,200 --> 00:53:02,400
Now the magnetization has a horizontal

1343
00:52:59,280 --> 00:53:04,079
component which we call MXY.

1344
00:53:02,400 --> 00:53:06,480
This component will oscillate and

1345
00:53:04,079 --> 00:53:08,079
produce an alternating magnetic field.

1346
00:53:06,480 --> 00:53:11,440
That is the field that induces a

1347
00:53:08,079 --> 00:53:12,720
measurable signal in the nearby coil.

1348
00:53:11,440 --> 00:53:15,440
Physically you can imagine the

1349
00:53:12,720 --> 00:53:17,359
magnetization vector as a magnetic bar.

1350
00:53:15,440 --> 00:53:19,359
If you keep flipping or rotating this

1351
00:53:17,359 --> 00:53:21,920
bar, the field it produces also keeps

1352
00:53:19,359 --> 00:53:23,680
changing. That changing field drives

1353
00:53:21,920 --> 00:53:26,800
current in the coil, which is exactly

1354
00:53:23,680 --> 00:53:28,960
what we detect as the MR signal.

1355
00:53:26,800 --> 00:53:31,200
The amplitude of the signal depends on

1356
00:53:28,960 --> 00:53:34,559
proton density. The more protons

1357
00:53:31,200 --> 00:53:36,720
available, the stronger the signal.

1358
00:53:34,559 --> 00:53:38,319
Now, after the excitation pulse ends,

1359
00:53:36,720 --> 00:53:40,480
the system will gradually return to

1360
00:53:38,319 --> 00:53:42,960
equilibrium. The Z component of

1361
00:53:40,480 --> 00:53:45,920
magnetization, MZ will recover to its

1362
00:53:42,960 --> 00:53:48,559
steady state value M0. This recovery is

1363
00:53:45,920 --> 00:53:50,160
governed by the T1 relaxation process,

1364
00:53:48,559 --> 00:53:52,240
sometimes called spin lattice

1365
00:53:50,160 --> 00:53:53,760
relaxation.

1366
00:53:52,240 --> 00:53:57,200
At the same time, the transverse

1367
00:53:53,760 --> 00:53:59,200
component MXY will decay towards zero.

1368
00:53:57,200 --> 00:54:01,359
This loss of coherence is governed by T2

1369
00:53:59,200 --> 00:54:03,280
relaxation, also called spin spin

1370
00:54:01,359 --> 00:54:06,160
relaxation.

1371
00:54:03,280 --> 00:54:08,960
So to summarize, T1 describes how the

1372
00:54:06,160 --> 00:54:11,440
longitudinal magnetization MZ returns to

1373
00:54:08,960 --> 00:54:14,000
equilibrium. T2 describes how the

1374
00:54:11,440 --> 00:54:15,680
transverse magnetization MXY decays to

1375
00:54:14,000 --> 00:54:17,599
zero.

1376
00:54:15,680 --> 00:54:19,520
Both of these effects are essential in

1377
00:54:17,599 --> 00:54:22,520
shaping the MR signal we actually

1378
00:54:19,520 --> 00:54:22,520
record.

1379
00:54:24,079 --> 00:54:28,079
Now let's talk about how the MR signal

1380
00:54:26,079 --> 00:54:30,319
is actually detected. When the

1381
00:54:28,079 --> 00:54:32,240
magnetization vector capital M is

1382
00:54:30,319 --> 00:54:34,240
flipped away from the Z-axis, it

1383
00:54:32,240 --> 00:54:37,359
develops a transverse component which we

1384
00:54:34,240 --> 00:54:39,680
call MXY. This transverse magnetization

1385
00:54:37,359 --> 00:54:42,400
does not remain static. It oscillates at

1386
00:54:39,680 --> 00:54:44,800
the resonance frequency.

1387
00:54:42,400 --> 00:54:47,040
That oscillation induces a sinosoidal

1388
00:54:44,800 --> 00:54:49,359
current in the radio frequency coil

1389
00:54:47,040 --> 00:54:52,079
exactly as predicted by Faraday's law of

1390
00:54:49,359 --> 00:54:53,680
electromagnetic induction.

1391
00:54:52,079 --> 00:54:56,800
The strength of this induced signal

1392
00:54:53,680 --> 00:54:58,880
depends directly on the size of MXY. The

1393
00:54:56,800 --> 00:55:00,960
larger the transverse component, the

1394
00:54:58,880 --> 00:55:02,960
stronger the oscillating magnetic field

1395
00:55:00,960 --> 00:55:05,440
and therefore the stronger the detected

1396
00:55:02,960 --> 00:55:07,520
voltage in the coil.

1397
00:55:05,440 --> 00:55:10,400
The maximum possible signal is reached

1398
00:55:07,520 --> 00:55:12,720
when the flip angle is 90°. At this

1399
00:55:10,400 --> 00:55:15,920
angle, the entire magnetization vector

1400
00:55:12,720 --> 00:55:18,480
lies in the xy plane. Meaning that mxy

1401
00:55:15,920 --> 00:55:20,720
is equal to m, the full equilibrium

1402
00:55:18,480 --> 00:55:23,280
magnetization.

1403
00:55:20,720 --> 00:55:25,440
This is why a 90° pulse is often used in

1404
00:55:23,280 --> 00:55:29,079
MRI. It gives the largest possible

1405
00:55:25,440 --> 00:55:29,079
signal for detection.

1406
00:55:30,640 --> 00:55:35,040
Once the radio frequency pulse is turned

1407
00:55:32,720 --> 00:55:36,880
off, the magnetization vector begins to

1408
00:55:35,040 --> 00:55:39,760
relax back toward the main magnetic

1409
00:55:36,880 --> 00:55:41,760
field, capital B knot. In this process,

1410
00:55:39,760 --> 00:55:43,520
the excess energy that was absorbed is

1411
00:55:41,760 --> 00:55:45,760
released.

1412
00:55:43,520 --> 00:55:48,640
As the system relaxes, the transverse

1413
00:55:45,760 --> 00:55:51,599
magnetization that is MXY begins to

1414
00:55:48,640 --> 00:55:54,160
decay. This decay produces a signal that

1415
00:55:51,599 --> 00:55:57,839
gradually decreases to zero. We call

1416
00:55:54,160 --> 00:55:59,839
this the free induction decay or FID.

1417
00:55:57,839 --> 00:56:02,400
The FID is the fundamental nuclear

1418
00:55:59,839 --> 00:56:04,240
magnetic resonance signal. It oscillates

1419
00:56:02,400 --> 00:56:06,000
at the resonance frequency and its

1420
00:56:04,240 --> 00:56:08,400
strength is proportional to the local

1421
00:56:06,000 --> 00:56:09,920
proton density.

1422
00:56:08,400 --> 00:56:11,440
In other words, the more protons you

1423
00:56:09,920 --> 00:56:13,599
have in a region, the stronger the

1424
00:56:11,440 --> 00:56:15,920
signal you record.

1425
00:56:13,599 --> 00:56:18,720
This decay curve shaped by relaxation

1426
00:56:15,920 --> 00:56:21,520
mechanisms T1 and T2 contains the raw

1427
00:56:18,720 --> 00:56:23,280
information that MRI uses. By capturing

1428
00:56:21,520 --> 00:56:25,280
and analyzing this signal, we can

1429
00:56:23,280 --> 00:56:28,920
reconstruct images that reveal tissue

1430
00:56:25,280 --> 00:56:28,920
structure and composition.

1431
00:56:30,559 --> 00:56:34,880
Now that we have covered how MRI signals

1432
00:56:32,880 --> 00:56:36,880
are generated and detected, the next

1433
00:56:34,880 --> 00:56:39,440
step is to understand how those signals

1434
00:56:36,880 --> 00:56:42,640
decay. This part is crucial because the

1435
00:56:39,440 --> 00:56:45,119
decay mechanisms, specifically T1 and T2

1436
00:56:42,640 --> 00:56:47,520
relaxation, are what ultimately give us

1437
00:56:45,119 --> 00:56:49,680
image contrast.

1438
00:56:47,520 --> 00:56:51,680
So in the final section of this lecture,

1439
00:56:49,680 --> 00:56:54,960
we will look more closely at the physics

1440
00:56:51,680 --> 00:56:57,440
behind T1 and T2. We will also see how

1441
00:56:54,960 --> 00:56:59,359
these relaxation times can be measured

1442
00:56:57,440 --> 00:57:01,599
and how pulse sequences such as

1443
00:56:59,359 --> 00:57:04,400
inversion recovery and spin echo are

1444
00:57:01,599 --> 00:57:06,240
designed to take advantage of them.

1445
00:57:04,400 --> 00:57:08,480
Up to this point, our discussion has

1446
00:57:06,240 --> 00:57:10,799
focused on the overall process of signal

1447
00:57:08,480 --> 00:57:12,559
generation and detection. But to move

1448
00:57:10,799 --> 00:57:15,680
from signals to images, we need to

1449
00:57:12,559 --> 00:57:18,000
understand relaxation. T1 and T2 are the

1450
00:57:15,680 --> 00:57:21,880
keys that translate raw MRI physics into

1451
00:57:18,000 --> 00:57:21,880
meaningful image contrast.

1452
00:57:23,440 --> 00:57:27,280
So now let's ask why does the MR signal

1453
00:57:25,599 --> 00:57:29,200
decay?

1454
00:57:27,280 --> 00:57:31,839
The answer is very much like the rolling

1455
00:57:29,200 --> 00:57:33,920
ball analogy. A ball on the ground slows

1456
00:57:31,839 --> 00:57:36,400
down because of resistance and friction.

1457
00:57:33,920 --> 00:57:38,319
In MRI, once we flip the magnetization

1458
00:57:36,400 --> 00:57:40,720
into procession, it cannot stay there

1459
00:57:38,319 --> 00:57:42,799
forever. Over time, it will naturally

1460
00:57:40,720 --> 00:57:46,160
return to its steady state aligned with

1461
00:57:42,799 --> 00:57:47,760
the main magnetic field B not.

1462
00:57:46,160 --> 00:57:50,960
This return happens through different

1463
00:57:47,760 --> 00:57:53,440
relaxation mechanisms. T1 relaxation,

1464
00:57:50,960 --> 00:57:55,680
also called longitudinal or spin lattice

1465
00:57:53,440 --> 00:57:58,079
relaxation, is when flipped nuclei

1466
00:57:55,680 --> 00:58:00,160
realign with the main magnetic field.

1467
00:57:58,079 --> 00:58:01,920
The energy they lose is given back to

1468
00:58:00,160 --> 00:58:03,680
the surrounding tissue as thermal

1469
00:58:01,920 --> 00:58:06,480
energy.

1470
00:58:03,680 --> 00:58:08,960
T2 relaxation, also called transverse or

1471
00:58:06,480 --> 00:58:10,960
spin spin relaxation, is when the nuclei

1472
00:58:08,960 --> 00:58:13,200
gradually lose phase coherence with one

1473
00:58:10,960 --> 00:58:15,359
another. Even though they were flipped

1474
00:58:13,200 --> 00:58:17,280
together, local differences in their

1475
00:58:15,359 --> 00:58:18,880
environment caused them to fall out of

1476
00:58:17,280 --> 00:58:21,200
step.

1477
00:58:18,880 --> 00:58:23,200
T2 star relaxation is an additional

1478
00:58:21,200 --> 00:58:25,839
effect that comes from imperfections in

1479
00:58:23,200 --> 00:58:28,240
the magnetic field itself. The field is

1480
00:58:25,839 --> 00:58:30,799
never perfectly uniform and small local

1481
00:58:28,240 --> 00:58:32,960
variations cause the spins to defphase

1482
00:58:30,799 --> 00:58:35,119
even faster.

1483
00:58:32,960 --> 00:58:37,520
This effect is especially important in

1484
00:58:35,119 --> 00:58:39,040
functional MRI where susceptibility

1485
00:58:37,520 --> 00:58:41,599
differences are actually used to

1486
00:58:39,040 --> 00:58:43,839
generate contrast.

1487
00:58:41,599 --> 00:58:46,960
The key point is that the MR signal we

1488
00:58:43,839 --> 00:58:49,760
detect, the NMR signal is proportional

1489
00:58:46,960 --> 00:58:54,079
to proton density but reduced by these

1490
00:58:49,760 --> 00:58:56,160
T1, T2 and T2 star factors.

1491
00:58:54,079 --> 00:58:59,440
And this is what gives MRI its powerful

1492
00:58:56,160 --> 00:59:01,200
contrast. For example, T1 weighting

1493
00:58:59,440 --> 00:59:03,200
helps us distinguish gray matter from

1494
00:59:01,200 --> 00:59:05,680
white matter.

1495
00:59:03,200 --> 00:59:08,880
T2 waiting highlights tissues and fluids

1496
00:59:05,680 --> 00:59:11,520
such as cerebrros spinal fluid.

1497
00:59:08,880 --> 00:59:13,520
T2 star waiting is especially useful for

1498
00:59:11,520 --> 00:59:16,160
functional MRI because it is sensitive

1499
00:59:13,520 --> 00:59:20,440
to magnetic susceptibility changes such

1500
00:59:16,160 --> 00:59:20,440
as those caused by blood oxygenation.

1501
00:59:20,480 --> 00:59:24,799
So signal decay is not a nuisance. In

1502
00:59:23,040 --> 00:59:28,760
fact, it's what makes MRI such a

1503
00:59:24,799 --> 00:59:28,760
versatile imaging tool.

1504
00:59:30,079 --> 00:59:33,839
Now let's take a closer look at the T1

1505
00:59:32,240 --> 00:59:35,920
effect.

1506
00:59:33,839 --> 00:59:37,680
T1 describes how the longitudinal

1507
00:59:35,920 --> 00:59:40,160
magnetization, that is the component

1508
00:59:37,680 --> 00:59:41,839
along the Z-axis, gradually returns to

1509
00:59:40,160 --> 00:59:45,280
its equilibrium value after being

1510
00:59:41,839 --> 00:59:46,960
disturbed by a radio frequency pulse.

1511
00:59:45,280 --> 00:59:49,920
On the left side of the figure, we see

1512
00:59:46,960 --> 00:59:52,000
what happens after a 90° pulse. In this

1513
00:59:49,920 --> 00:59:54,079
case, the longitudinal magnetization,

1514
00:59:52,000 --> 00:59:55,920
which we call MZ, has been tipped

1515
00:59:54,079 --> 00:59:58,319
entirely into the transverse plane. So,

1516
00:59:55,920 --> 01:00:00,160
it starts at zero.

1517
00:59:58,319 --> 01:00:02,640
Over time, it recovers back toward its

1518
01:00:00,160 --> 01:00:05,920
equilibrium value, which we call M. and

1519
01:00:02,640 --> 01:00:08,480
it does so in an exponential fashion.

1520
01:00:05,920 --> 01:00:11,520
On the right side, we see the case of a

1521
01:00:08,480 --> 01:00:13,440
180° pulse. Here, the longitudinal

1522
01:00:11,520 --> 01:00:16,319
magnetization is flipped completely

1523
01:00:13,440 --> 01:00:17,839
upside down, starting at negative m.

1524
01:00:16,319 --> 01:00:20,880
From there, it also recovers

1525
01:00:17,839 --> 01:00:22,400
exponentially back to m.

1526
01:00:20,880 --> 01:00:25,119
This exponential recovery is the

1527
01:00:22,400 --> 01:00:27,359
hallmark of T1 relaxation. The recovery

1528
01:00:25,119 --> 01:00:29,280
speed depends on the tissue type because

1529
01:00:27,359 --> 01:00:31,280
different tissues exchange energy with

1530
01:00:29,280 --> 01:00:34,640
their environment, the so-called spin

1531
01:00:31,280 --> 01:00:37,520
lattice interaction at different rates.

1532
01:00:34,640 --> 01:00:39,839
So to summarize, T1 tells us how quickly

1533
01:00:37,520 --> 01:00:42,880
a tissue's magnetization realign with

1534
01:00:39,839 --> 01:00:44,880
the main magnetic field B 0. And these

1535
01:00:42,880 --> 01:00:49,880
differences in T1 times are one of the

1536
01:00:44,880 --> 01:00:49,880
key sources of image contrast in MRI.

1537
01:00:51,520 --> 01:00:55,599
Now let's talk about the T2 effect which

1538
01:00:53,520 --> 01:00:57,520
is also called transverse relaxation or

1539
01:00:55,599 --> 01:00:59,680
defasing.

1540
01:00:57,520 --> 01:01:01,680
After we apply a 90° pulse, the net

1541
01:00:59,680 --> 01:01:04,799
magnetization lies entirely in the

1542
01:01:01,680 --> 01:01:06,640
transverse plane along the xy plane. At

1543
01:01:04,799 --> 01:01:08,799
that initial moment, all of the tiny

1544
01:01:06,640 --> 01:01:10,640
magnetic moments of individual protons

1545
01:01:08,799 --> 01:01:12,559
are lined up together pointing in the

1546
01:01:10,640 --> 01:01:14,640
same direction.

1547
01:01:12,559 --> 01:01:16,640
But over time, each of those protons

1548
01:01:14,640 --> 01:01:19,200
experiences slightly different local

1549
01:01:16,640 --> 01:01:20,960
magnetic fields. Some of them precess a

1550
01:01:19,200 --> 01:01:22,960
little faster and others precess a

1551
01:01:20,960 --> 01:01:24,880
little slower. As a result, they

1552
01:01:22,960 --> 01:01:26,480
gradually drift out of phase with one

1553
01:01:24,880 --> 01:01:28,240
another.

1554
01:01:26,480 --> 01:01:30,720
When that happens, their contributions

1555
01:01:28,240 --> 01:01:32,480
begin to cancel out. The net transverse

1556
01:01:30,720 --> 01:01:34,960
magnetization shrinks even though each

1557
01:01:32,480 --> 01:01:36,559
proton is still spinning.

1558
01:01:34,960 --> 01:01:38,960
On the graph at the bottom, you can see

1559
01:01:36,559 --> 01:01:41,119
this process clearly. The transverse

1560
01:01:38,960 --> 01:01:43,359
magnetization starts at its maximum

1561
01:01:41,119 --> 01:01:45,440
value and then decays exponentially

1562
01:01:43,359 --> 01:01:47,839
towards zero as the moments become more

1563
01:01:45,440 --> 01:01:50,400
and more defased.

1564
01:01:47,839 --> 01:01:52,799
This is the essence of the T2 relaxation

1565
01:01:50,400 --> 01:01:54,799
process. It measures how quickly the

1566
01:01:52,799 --> 01:01:56,880
spins lose phase coherence in the

1567
01:01:54,799 --> 01:01:59,880
transverse plane leading to signal

1568
01:01:56,880 --> 01:01:59,880
decay.

1569
01:02:01,520 --> 01:02:06,400
At this stage, we can summarize how T1

1570
01:02:03,920 --> 01:02:10,079
and T2 relaxation describe the time

1571
01:02:06,400 --> 01:02:11,839
evolution of magnetization in MRI.

1572
01:02:10,079 --> 01:02:14,240
First, consider the longitudinal

1573
01:02:11,839 --> 01:02:16,319
component, which we usually call MZ.

1574
01:02:14,240 --> 01:02:18,480
After a radio frequency pulse, it does

1575
01:02:16,319 --> 01:02:20,400
not instantly return to equilibrium.

1576
01:02:18,480 --> 01:02:23,200
Instead, it recovers gradually following

1577
01:02:20,400 --> 01:02:25,680
an exponential curve.

1578
01:02:23,200 --> 01:02:29,599
Mathematically, we say that mz of time=

1579
01:02:25,680 --> 01:02:32,240
multiplied 1 - e to the power of t over

1580
01:02:29,599 --> 01:02:35,280
t1. In plain words, this means the

1581
01:02:32,240 --> 01:02:37,200
recovery depends on a time constant t1,

1582
01:02:35,280 --> 01:02:40,640
which tells us how quickly the spins

1583
01:02:37,200 --> 01:02:42,640
realign with the main magnetic field.

1584
01:02:40,640 --> 01:02:45,599
Next for the transverse components which

1585
01:02:42,640 --> 01:02:47,520
are mx and my these decay over time.

1586
01:02:45,599 --> 01:02:50,079
Their rate of decay is described by the

1587
01:02:47,520 --> 01:02:53,280
time constant t2.

1588
01:02:50,079 --> 01:02:59,920
The equations are written as dmx / dt =

1589
01:02:53,280 --> 01:03:01,839
minus mx / t2 and dmy / dt = - t2. In

1590
01:02:59,920 --> 01:03:04,240
other words, both x and y components

1591
01:03:01,839 --> 01:03:07,040
shrink exponentially towards zero at a

1592
01:03:04,240 --> 01:03:09,440
rate determined by t2.

1593
01:03:07,040 --> 01:03:12,640
So together T1 and T2 give us a

1594
01:03:09,440 --> 01:03:14,480
semi-quantitative model for MRI. T1

1595
01:03:12,640 --> 01:03:17,200
governs how fast the longitudinal

1596
01:03:14,480 --> 01:03:19,280
magnetization recovers and T2 governs

1597
01:03:17,200 --> 01:03:21,839
how fast the transverse magnetization

1598
01:03:19,280 --> 01:03:23,760
disappears. Both processes follow

1599
01:03:21,839 --> 01:03:26,720
exponential curves but with different

1600
01:03:23,760 --> 01:03:29,119
time constants.

1601
01:03:26,720 --> 01:03:31,760
Here

1602
01:03:29,119 --> 01:03:34,160
we have a summary table of T1 and T2

1603
01:03:31,760 --> 01:03:36,640
relaxation times for different tissues

1604
01:03:34,160 --> 01:03:38,480
measured at a field strength of 1.5

1605
01:03:36,640 --> 01:03:41,440
Tesla.

1606
01:03:38,480 --> 01:03:44,480
For fat, the T1 relaxation time is about

1607
01:03:41,440 --> 01:03:46,480
260 milliseconds and the T2 is about 80

1608
01:03:44,480 --> 01:03:49,280
milliseconds.

1609
01:03:46,480 --> 01:03:51,440
For muscle, T1 is around 870

1610
01:03:49,280 --> 01:03:54,079
milliseconds while T2 is much shorter,

1611
01:03:51,440 --> 01:03:56,640
about 45 milliseconds.

1612
01:03:54,079 --> 01:03:59,520
In the brain, gray matter has a T1 of

1613
01:03:56,640 --> 01:04:02,000
about 900 milliseconds and a T2 of about

1614
01:03:59,520 --> 01:04:04,799
100 milliseconds. White matter is

1615
01:04:02,000 --> 01:04:06,960
slightly shorter with a T1 of about 780

1616
01:04:04,799 --> 01:04:09,039
milliseconds and a T2 of about 90

1617
01:04:06,960 --> 01:04:11,359
milliseconds.

1618
01:04:09,039 --> 01:04:13,520
The liver shows a T1 of about 500

1619
01:04:11,359 --> 01:04:15,520
milliseconds and a T2 of about 40

1620
01:04:13,520 --> 01:04:17,760
milliseconds.

1621
01:04:15,520 --> 01:04:20,559
Finally, cerebral spinal fluid has the

1622
01:04:17,760 --> 01:04:24,559
longest times by far. a t1 of about

1623
01:04:20,559 --> 01:04:26,559
2,400 milliseconds and a t2 of about 160

1624
01:04:24,559 --> 01:04:28,480
milliseconds.

1625
01:04:26,559 --> 01:04:29,839
These values illustrate a key point.

1626
01:04:28,480 --> 01:04:32,160
Different tissues have different

1627
01:04:29,839 --> 01:04:34,480
relaxation times and that difference is

1628
01:04:32,160 --> 01:04:38,839
what gives MRI its powerful ability to

1629
01:04:34,480 --> 01:04:38,839
generate contrast between tissues.

1630
01:04:40,480 --> 01:04:45,760
Now let's distinguish between T2, T2

1631
01:04:42,880 --> 01:04:47,200
prime and T2 star. The loss of phase

1632
01:04:45,760 --> 01:04:49,039
coherence in the transverse

1633
01:04:47,200 --> 01:04:51,680
magnetization can arise from two

1634
01:04:49,039 --> 01:04:54,480
different mechanisms. The first is the

1635
01:04:51,680 --> 01:04:57,280
so-called pure T2 decay which comes from

1636
01:04:54,480 --> 01:04:59,839
intrinsic spin spin interactions inside

1637
01:04:57,280 --> 01:05:02,000
the tissue. This is a physiological and

1638
01:04:59,839 --> 01:05:04,160
biological effect and it represents the

1639
01:05:02,000 --> 01:05:07,039
fundamental limit of how long spins can

1640
01:05:04,160 --> 01:05:08,720
stay in phase with one another.

1641
01:05:07,039 --> 01:05:10,880
The second contribution comes from

1642
01:05:08,720 --> 01:05:13,280
spatial variations in the magnetic field

1643
01:05:10,880 --> 01:05:15,760
strength inside the body. In practice,

1644
01:05:13,280 --> 01:05:17,440
no magnet is perfectly uniform. There

1645
01:05:15,760 --> 01:05:20,000
are always small imperfections in the

1646
01:05:17,440 --> 01:05:21,839
main field B 0.

1647
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:23,359
In addition, different tissues have

1648
