susceptibilities, especially at

1650
01:05:25,200 --> 01:05:30,240
boundaries between air and tissue or

1651
01:05:27,520 --> 01:05:32,559
bone and tissue. These local variations

1652
01:05:30,240 --> 01:05:34,559
cause spins to accumulate extraphase

1653
01:05:32,559 --> 01:05:36,880
shifts, further accelerating the loss of

1654
01:05:34,559 --> 01:05:40,000
coherence. This additional contribution

1655
01:05:36,880 --> 01:05:41,839
is represented by T2 prime.

1656
01:05:40,000 --> 01:05:44,000
When we put these together, the overall

1657
01:05:41,839 --> 01:05:46,720
transverse relaxation time we observe is

1658
01:05:44,000 --> 01:05:48,960
called T2 star. Mathematically, the rate

1659
01:05:46,720 --> 01:05:52,480
of decay of T2 star is the sum of the

1660
01:05:48,960 --> 01:05:56,240
rates of T2 and T2 prime. That is 1 / T2

1661
01:05:52,480 --> 01:05:59,200
star= 1 / T2 + 1 over T2 prime.

1662
01:05:56,240 --> 01:06:01,760
So in summary, T2 reflects fundamental

1663
01:05:59,200 --> 01:06:04,079
spin spin interactions.

1664
01:06:01,760 --> 01:06:06,880
T2 prime reflects field and homogeneity

1665
01:06:04,079 --> 01:06:09,280
and susceptibility effects.

1666
01:06:06,880 --> 01:06:11,280
T2 star combines both and it is the

1667
01:06:09,280 --> 01:06:15,400
effective decay time we actually measure

1668
01:06:11,280 --> 01:06:15,400
in many MRI sequences.

1669
01:06:17,200 --> 01:06:22,960
Now let's look at how T1 can be measured

1670
01:06:19,599 --> 01:06:25,920
using the inversion recovery method.

1671
01:06:22,960 --> 01:06:28,079
The idea is to start with a 180° pulse

1672
01:06:25,920 --> 01:06:29,920
which flips the net magnetization

1673
01:06:28,079 --> 01:06:32,400
completely upside down along the

1674
01:06:29,920 --> 01:06:34,160
negative Z-axis.

1675
01:06:32,400 --> 01:06:36,000
Once it is inverted, we allow it to

1676
01:06:34,160 --> 01:06:38,559
recover toward equilibrium during a

1677
01:06:36,000 --> 01:06:40,319
delay time which we call TOAO. During

1678
01:06:38,559 --> 01:06:43,039
this period, the longitudinal

1679
01:06:40,319 --> 01:06:45,039
magnetization gradually regrows toward

1680
01:06:43,039 --> 01:06:47,280
its steady state following the

1681
01:06:45,039 --> 01:06:48,960
exponential recovery curve we discussed

1682
01:06:47,280 --> 01:06:51,440
earlier.

1683
01:06:48,960 --> 01:06:54,319
At the end of the delay, we apply a 90°

1684
01:06:51,440 --> 01:06:56,480
pulse. This flips whatever longitudinal

1685
01:06:54,319 --> 01:06:58,880
magnetization has recovered into the

1686
01:06:56,480 --> 01:07:01,200
transverse plane where it produces a

1687
01:06:58,880 --> 01:07:03,440
measurable signal.

1688
01:07:01,200 --> 01:07:05,760
By repeating this process with different

1689
01:07:03,440 --> 01:07:09,440
values of toao, we can track how the

1690
01:07:05,760 --> 01:07:11,599
magnetization regrows over time.

1691
01:07:09,440 --> 01:07:14,720
Mathematically, the detected signal

1692
01:07:11,599 --> 01:07:20,400
follows the expression s of toao equals

1693
01:07:14,720 --> 01:07:22,079
m 0 * the quant 1 - 2 * e^ minus tow.

1694
01:07:20,400 --> 01:07:24,880
By fitting this recovery curve, we

1695
01:07:22,079 --> 01:07:26,480
obtain the t1 relaxation time. In

1696
01:07:24,880 --> 01:07:28,559
practice, this method gives a very

1697
01:07:26,480 --> 01:07:30,319
robust way to measure T1 across

1698
01:07:28,559 --> 01:07:32,720
different tissues and it is the basis

1699
01:07:30,319 --> 01:07:35,960
for many T1 weighted imaging protocols

1700
01:07:32,720 --> 01:07:35,960
in MRI.

1701
01:07:37,680 --> 01:07:42,720
Now, let's visualize what's happening in

1702
01:07:39,599 --> 01:07:44,640
an inversion recovery sequence.

1703
01:07:42,720 --> 01:07:46,799
We start with the net magnetization

1704
01:07:44,640 --> 01:07:50,400
pointing up along the Z-axis at its

1705
01:07:46,799 --> 01:07:52,559
equilibrium value M0. Then we apply a

1706
01:07:50,400 --> 01:07:55,920
180°ree pulse which flips it completely

1707
01:07:52,559 --> 01:07:57,359
upside down to minus m0.

1708
01:07:55,920 --> 01:07:59,280
From this inverted state, the

1709
01:07:57,359 --> 01:08:01,760
magnetization begins to relax back

1710
01:07:59,280 --> 01:08:03,839
toward equilibrium. Over time, the

1711
01:08:01,760 --> 01:08:07,680
longitudinal component regrows along the

1712
01:08:03,839 --> 01:08:09,760
Z-axis following the T1 recovery curve.

1713
01:08:07,680 --> 01:08:13,119
At some chosen inversion time, which we

1714
01:08:09,760 --> 01:08:14,799
call TI, we apply a 90° pulse. This

1715
01:08:13,119 --> 01:08:16,719
rotates whatever longitudinal

1716
01:08:14,799 --> 01:08:19,199
magnetization has recovered into the

1717
01:08:16,719 --> 01:08:21,040
transverse plane. Once in the transverse

1718
01:08:19,199 --> 01:08:23,759
plane, it generates a measurable free

1719
01:08:21,040 --> 01:08:26,960
induction decay or FID signal that is

1720
01:08:23,759 --> 01:08:28,880
subject to T2 star decay.

1721
01:08:26,960 --> 01:08:30,719
By repeating this process with different

1722
01:08:28,880 --> 01:08:32,400
inversion times and recording the

1723
01:08:30,719 --> 01:08:35,120
signals, we can map out the full

1724
01:08:32,400 --> 01:08:38,960
recovery curve. Then using a logarithmic

1725
01:08:35,120 --> 01:08:41,759
fit, we extract the T1 relaxation time.

1726
01:08:38,960 --> 01:08:44,159
So in short, this diagram shows how the

1727
01:08:41,759 --> 01:08:46,640
180°ree inversion, the recovery period,

1728
01:08:44,159 --> 01:08:51,239
and the 90° readout pulse together make

1729
01:08:46,640 --> 01:08:51,239
it possible to measure T1 directly.

1730
01:08:52,880 --> 01:08:58,640
Now let's look at how we measure T2

1731
01:08:55,040 --> 01:09:01,120
relaxation using the spin echo method.

1732
01:08:58,640 --> 01:09:03,199
We begin with a 90° pulse that tips the

1733
01:09:01,120 --> 01:09:05,600
net magnetization into the transverse

1734
01:09:03,199 --> 01:09:07,839
plane. Right away, the spins begin to

1735
01:09:05,600 --> 01:09:11,199
defphase because of small differences in

1736
01:09:07,839 --> 01:09:13,279
their local magnetic environments.

1737
01:09:11,199 --> 01:09:15,120
Faster spins move ahead, slower spins

1738
01:09:13,279 --> 01:09:16,960
lag, and the overall signal decays

1739
01:09:15,120 --> 01:09:19,359
quickly with a time constant that looks

1740
01:09:16,960 --> 01:09:21,040
like T2 star.

1741
01:09:19,359 --> 01:09:24,400
But here is the clever trick. At a

1742
01:09:21,040 --> 01:09:26,319
certain time, we apply a 180° pulse.

1743
01:09:24,400 --> 01:09:27,679
This flips all the spins over so that

1744
01:09:26,319 --> 01:09:29,600
the ones that were leading are now

1745
01:09:27,679 --> 01:09:31,839
behind and the ones that were lagging

1746
01:09:29,600 --> 01:09:33,679
are now in front.

1747
01:09:31,839 --> 01:09:35,520
As time continues, these spins recon

1748
01:09:33,679 --> 01:09:38,239
converge and at a later time they come

1749
01:09:35,520 --> 01:09:40,239
back into phase. When that happens, we

1750
01:09:38,239 --> 01:09:42,640
see the spins add constructively and

1751
01:09:40,239 --> 01:09:44,719
produce a strong signal known as the

1752
01:09:42,640 --> 01:09:46,560
spin echo.

1753
01:09:44,719 --> 01:09:49,199
The height of this echo decays with the

1754
01:09:46,560 --> 01:09:51,440
true T2 relaxation time, not with T2

1755
01:09:49,199 --> 01:09:53,279
star. By repeating the sequence with

1756
01:09:51,440 --> 01:09:55,760
different time delays, we can track how

1757
01:09:53,279 --> 01:09:59,440
quickly the echo signal diminishes and

1758
01:09:55,760 --> 01:10:00,960
from that extract the T2 constant.

1759
01:09:59,440 --> 01:10:02,960
This technique is both simple and

1760
01:10:00,960 --> 01:10:05,280
powerful. It cancels out static and

1761
01:10:02,960 --> 01:10:07,920
homogeneities in the magnetic field and

1762
01:10:05,280 --> 01:10:12,679
isolates the true spin spin relaxation

1763
01:10:07,920 --> 01:10:12,679
which is exactly what T2 represents.

